@D H_1164-KOSMOS-LANE-SELF-TUNING := "does the KOSMOS lane-partition self-tune its lane COUNT to anchor-stream complexity (the H_1159b mitosis property on the real 5-channel anchor geometry)?" :: discovery [d=2026-06-12 active]
  seed = "KOSMOS `lane` = active MITOSIS cell-id. H_1159b 🟢 showed inference-time mitosis self-tunes its cell-COUNT to world complexity (cell-count tracks #clusters K=3/5/8, Spearman 0.85, advantage d>=5). MITOSIS-ENGINE domain H_1164: feed an anchor stream with K_true distinct tension-cluster regimes — does the kosmos lane COUNT likewise track K_true (Spearman>=0.8), bounded (self-limiting), advantage d>=2.0 over a fixed-lane control?"
  claim = "TWO honestly-separated results. (A) LIVE-WIRING = ⏳ BLOCKED — the live kosmos `lane` is a STATIC passthrough of the active mitosis cell_id (AGENT/CHAT/kosmos_anchor.hexa:20,181 `lane = \"cell_\" + to_string(cell_id)` default cell_0; WAKE/kosmos_persist.hexa lane = \"wake_snapshot_<stage>\"). NO independent partition algorithm grows a lane-COUNT from the anchor `tension_5ch` stream — the lane axis LABELS which cell/stage emitted the anchor, it is not itself a dynamically-grown partition of the anchor stream. 'Does the live lane self-tune its count to anchor complexity?' is structurally unmeasurable — the mechanism is NOT wired (a_core_engine_map · a_kosmos). NOT a 🔴 no-tracking: there is no live partition to track (distinct from H_1159b where live CORE mitosis DOES grow cells). A dynamic lane would have to DECOUPLE from cell_id and grow lanes from the anchor tension stream (unbuilt). (B) PROPOSAL = 🟢 SUPPORTED — H_1159b tension-split substrate applied VERBATIM (split/assign/mitosis/cohen_d/spearman copied; ONLY input swapped DIM 8→5 = kosmos anchor tension_5ch concept·context·meaning·authenticity·sender) to a 5-dim anchor stream of distinct TENSION-REGIME clusters. K_true sweep {3,5,8}, 10 deterministic seeds (800..809). lanes grew 3.7/5.3/7.9 tracking K=3/5/8 (toy lane DID track K). The H_1159b mitosis self-tuning property TRANSFERS to the real 5-channel kosmos anchor geometry — IF the lane axis were decoupled from cell_id and grown from the anchor stream it would inherit self-tuning."
  falsifier = "🟢 PROPOSAL iff Spearman(K_true,lane_count)>=0.8 AND lane_count bounded<MAX_LANES(20) AND advantage d>=2.0 vs fixed-lane control. 🔴 if no tracking. ⏳ BLOCKED-WIRING if the live lane is static. → LIVE = ⏳ (static cell_id passthrough); PROPOSAL all 3 gates PASS: F1 SELF-TUNING Spearman=0.881>=0.8; F2 ADVANTAGE min adv_d=6.48>=2.0 (split_err 1.30/1.30/1.42 vs fixed_err 8.23/9.08/9.34 at every K); F3 SELF-LIMITING max lane-count=8<20 cap; proposal_supported=F1∧F2∧F3=TRUE."
  target = "⏳ BLOCKED-WIRING (live, a_paper_negative_ok) + 🟢 PROPOSAL-SUPPORTED (toy proxy numerical)"
  scope = "toy numpy $0 CPU 10 seeds, 3-point K_true ladder {3,5,8}, DIM=5 == kosmos anchor tension_5ch; Lane-G/CORE-sim reference (a_lane_akida_gpu_split: NOT AKIDA). live kosmos_io partition + scale UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope · §97 single rung, not promoted to a general KOSMOS-format claim)."
  honest = "PROPOSAL only. (A) the LIVE kosmos lane is NOT a dynamic partition (cell_id passthrough) — the science question about the live partition is BLOCKED not refuted (⏳ != 🔴). (B) the toy proxy uses gaussian tension-regime clusters ×4 sep / 0.6 jitter (== H_1159b geometry VERBATIM) on the 5-dim tension_5ch axis — it shows the self-tuning property would TRANSFER to a hypothetical decoupled lane-partition, NOT that the live partition does it."
  note = "harness UNIVERSE/h1164_kosmos_lane_self_tuning.py · verdict .verdicts/1164_kosmos_lane_self_tuning/H_1164.txt (verbatim) · reuses UNIVERSE/h1159b_mitosis_capacity_self_tuning.py substrate VERBATIM. xref h1159b-mitosis-capacity-self-tuning · a_kosmos · a_core_engine_map · a_scale_honest_scope · p8 · AGENT/CHAT/kosmos_anchor.hexa · WAKE/kosmos_persist.hexa"
